payload/cx/  --  shared immutable legacy LG GStreamer payload
================================================================

Profiles:

    cx-armv7-gst114       inherited CX mechanism (not verified by this project)
    webos22-o22-gst118    exact-firmware C2/G2 opt-in (hardware verification NO)

The release workflow generates this directory from exactly four tracked files
in the repository root's gst/ directory:

    payload/cx/libgstlibav.so
    payload/cx/libgstisomp4.so
    payload/cx/libgstisomp4_1_8.so
    payload/cx/libgstmatroska.so

From the repository root, the equivalent local packaging step is:

    cp -f gst/*.so webos25/app/payload/cx/

These are the shipping dts_restore binaries built from LG's GStreamer 1.14.4
sources: gst-plugins-good for Matroska/isomp4 and gst-libav for dca decode with
the forced stereo-integer downmix. The payload itself is measured ELF32 ARM
EABI5 soft-float. This project has not captured a stock CX loader/e_flags pair
on hardware, and no rooted C2/G2 was available for this implementation.

The profiles share only these immutable package files:

* CX copies them under /var/lib/webosbrew/dtsenabler/cx/gst/, uses the inherited
  /var/lib/webosbrew/init.d/restore_dts hook, refreshes the registry, and raises
  avdec_dca from 0 to 290.
* C2 uses dedicated /var/lib/webosbrew/dtsenabler/c2 state and the authenticated
  regular hook /var/lib/webosbrew/init.d/restore_dts_c2. It is offered only for
  the exact global W22O 04.40.93/04.40.93.01 identity, ABI, GStreamer 1.18.2,
  and stock SHA-256 set documented in ../../README.md. It always requires the
  two-step experimental opt-in and never becomes hardware verified from a
  userspace self-test.

All four files must be present in the package. C2 binds libgstisomp4_1_8.so only
when that stock target exists. No legacy libgstmpegtsdemux.so is tracked, so the
C2 capability is MKV/MP4 DTS only, never TS/M2TS or TrueHD.

WARNING: applying these 1.14 libraries to an unmatched target can break media
playback. The service refuses every identity/version/hash mismatch, every
diagnostic B2/C3/B3 profile, and all unknown profiles; GStreamer version alone
never authorizes C2.

Generated payload .so files are NOT committed (see ../../.gitignore). The four
legacy files are LGPL-2.1-or-later; include the license and corresponding-source
provenance in licenses/NOTICE.md with every distributed .ipk.
